{
  $schema: 'https://docs.renovatebot.com/renovate-schema.json',
  description: [
    'Digest pinning comes from the docker:pinDigests preset, so there is deliberately no top-level docker block. The old one claimed to force amd64 pulls and never did: Renovate pins the manifest-list digest, so each node still pulls its own platform. Its versioning: docker was already the default, and as migrated it overrode the preset\'s pinDigests: false for argocd, devcontainer, helmv3 and pyenv. If devcontainer digests are ever wanted, ask for them explicitly rather than reinstating a global override. Kept here because Renovate\'s config migration (#2312) strips JSON5 comments. Full history in #2123.',
  ],
  extends: [
    'config:recommended',
    'docker:enableMajor',
    'docker:pinDigests',
    ':disableRateLimiting',
    ':dependencyDashboard',
    ':semanticCommits',
    ':automergeBranch',
  ],
  dependencyDashboard: {
    enabled: true,
    title: 'Renovate Dashboard 🤖',
  },
  suppressNotifications: [
    'prEditedNotification',
    'prIgnoreNotification',
  ],
  rebaseWhen: 'conflicted',
  // Without a timezone the weekend is UTC, which ran from Saturday mid-morning
  // to Monday mid-morning here.
  timezone: 'Australia/Sydney',
  schedule: [
    'every weekend',
  ],
  ignorePaths: [
    '**/*.sops.*',
    // Apps whose ks.yaml is commented out of their namespace kustomization.
    // Their bumps change nothing live. Remove the line if one is re-enabled.
    'kubernetes/apps/media/jellyfin/**',
    'kubernetes/apps/media/mylar/**',
    'kubernetes/apps/observability/overseerr-exporter/**',
    'kubernetes/apps/utilities/pdi-keepalive/**',
  ],
  flux: {
    managerFilePatterns: [
      '/(^|/)kubernetes/.+\\.ya?ml(?:\\.j2)?$/',
    ],
  },
  'helm-values': {
    managerFilePatterns: [
      '/(^|/)kubernetes/.+\\.ya?ml(?:\\.j2)?$/',
    ],
  },
  helmfile: {
    managerFilePatterns: [
      '/(^|/)helmfile\\.ya?ml(?:\\.j2)?$/',
    ],
  },
  kubernetes: {
    managerFilePatterns: [
      '/(^|/)kubernetes/.+\\.ya?ml(?:\\.j2)?$/',
    ],
  },
  kustomize: {
    managerFilePatterns: [
      '/(^|/)kustomization\\.ya?ml(?:\\.j2)?$/',
    ],
  },
  pip_requirements: {
    managerFilePatterns: [
      '/(^|/)[\\w-]*requirements(-\\w+)?\\.(txt|pip)(?:\\.j2)?$/',
    ],
  },
  commitMessageTopic: '{{depName}}',
  commitMessageExtra: 'to {{newVersion}}',
  commitMessageSuffix: '',
  packageRules: [
    {
      description: [
        'Disable digest pinning for OCIRepository resources - they do not support digests',
      ],
      matchManagers: [
        'flux',
      ],
      matchDatasources: [
        'docker',
      ],
      matchFileNames: [
        '**/ocirepository.yaml',
        '**/flux.yaml',
      ],
      pinDigests: false,
    },
    {
      description: [
        'Pin GitHub Actions to a commit SHA and keep the pin current',
      ],
      matchManagers: [
        'github-actions',
      ],
      pinDigests: true,
    },
    {
      description: [
        'Auto merge Github Actions',
      ],
      matchManagers: [
        'github-actions',
      ],
      automerge: true,
      automergeType: 'branch',
      ignoreTests: true,
      matchUpdateTypes: [
        'minor',
        'patch',
      ],
    },
    {
      description: [
        'Flux Group',
      ],
      groupName: 'Flux',
      matchDatasources: [
        'docker',
        'github-tags',
      ],
      versioning: 'semver',
      group: {
        commitMessageTopic: '{{{groupName}}} group',
      },
      separateMinorPatch: true,
      matchPackageNames: [
        '/fluxcd/',
      ],
    },
    {
      description: [
        'Talos Group',
      ],
      groupName: 'Talos',
      matchDatasources: [
        'docker',
      ],
      group: {
        commitMessageTopic: '{{{groupName}}} group',
      },
      separateMinorPatch: true,
      matchPackageNames: [
        '/siderolabs/talosctl/',
        '/siderolabs/installer/',
      ],
    },
    {
      description: [
        'Pin emqx-operator to 2.2.x - 2.3.0+ requires EMQX Enterprise 5.9+ with licence for clustering',
      ],
      matchDatasources: [
        'helm',
      ],
      matchPackageNames: [
        'emqx-operator',
      ],
      allowedVersions: '<2.3.0',
    },
    {
      description: [
        'nocodb moved from 0.x to date versioning (0.301.5 -> 2026.04.0 in 2026-04). Renovate 44 added maxMajorIncrement with a default of 500 and treats that as a major jump of 2026, so it silently skipped every release since. Confirmed 2026-11-03 with a local dry-run: "Skipping nocodb/nocodb@2026.10.1 because major increment 2026 exceeds maxMajorIncrement 500". Remove once the pin is on a 2026.x tag.',
      ],
      matchDatasources: [
        'docker',
      ],
      matchPackageNames: [
        'nocodb/nocodb',
      ],
      maxMajorIncrement: 0,
    },
    {
      description: [
        'Hold sonarr on v4 until upstream ships v5 as stable: every v5 release is a prerelease, and v5 migrates the database so a revert means a restore. Remove once v5 is stable.',
      ],
      matchDatasources: [
        'docker',
      ],
      matchPackageNames: [
        'ghcr.io/home-operations/sonarr',
      ],
      allowedVersions: '<5',
    },
    {
      description: [
        'Keep n8n on the stable release line. n8n ships three lines at once: 2.45.x is stable (the stable and latest tags both point at it), 2.46.x is beta (the beta and next tags), and 3.0.x is on no channel at all and has not moved since 2026-10-28 while the other three shipped. Renovate cannot see this, because ignoreUnstable only filters semver prerelease strings and 2.46.3 is clean semver, so without this cap it offers the beta and the major as ordinary updates. n8n also runs DB migrations on upgrade, so a revert is a Postgres restore rather than a rollback. Raise the cap deliberately when 2.46 becomes stable.',
      ],
      matchDatasources: [
        'docker',
      ],
      matchPackageNames: [
        'docker.io/n8nio/n8n',
      ],
      allowedVersions: '<2.46',
    },
    {
      matchDatasources: [
        'helm',
      ],
      commitMessageTopic: 'chart {{depName}}',
    },
    {
      matchDatasources: [
        'docker',
      ],
      commitMessageTopic: 'image {{depName}}',
    },
    {
      matchDatasources: [
        'docker',
      ],
      matchUpdateTypes: [
        'major',
      ],
      commitMessagePrefix: 'feat(container)!: ',
    },
    {
      matchDatasources: [
        'docker',
      ],
      matchUpdateTypes: [
        'minor',
      ],
      semanticCommitType: 'feat',
      semanticCommitScope: 'container',
    },
    {
      matchDatasources: [
        'docker',
      ],
      matchUpdateTypes: [
        'patch',
      ],
      semanticCommitType: 'fix',
      semanticCommitScope: 'container',
    },
    {
      matchDatasources: [
        'docker',
      ],
      matchUpdateTypes: [
        'digest',
      ],
      semanticCommitType: 'chore',
      semanticCommitScope: 'container',
    },
    {
      matchDatasources: [
        'helm',
      ],
      matchUpdateTypes: [
        'major',
      ],
      commitMessagePrefix: 'feat(helm)!: ',
    },
    {
      matchDatasources: [
        'helm',
      ],
      matchUpdateTypes: [
        'minor',
      ],
      semanticCommitType: 'feat',
      semanticCommitScope: 'helm',
    },
    {
      matchDatasources: [
        'helm',
      ],
      matchUpdateTypes: [
        'patch',
      ],
      semanticCommitType: 'fix',
      semanticCommitScope: 'helm',
    },
    {
      matchDatasources: [
        'github-releases',
        'github-tags',
      ],
      matchUpdateTypes: [
        'major',
      ],
      commitMessagePrefix: 'feat(github-release)!: ',
    },
    {
      matchDatasources: [
        'github-releases',
        'github-tags',
      ],
      matchUpdateTypes: [
        'minor',
      ],
      semanticCommitType: 'feat',
      semanticCommitScope: 'github-release',
    },
    {
      matchDatasources: [
        'github-releases',
        'github-tags',
      ],
      matchUpdateTypes: [
        'patch',
      ],
      semanticCommitType: 'fix',
      semanticCommitScope: 'github-release',
    },
    {
      matchManagers: [
        'github-actions',
      ],
      matchUpdateTypes: [
        'major',
      ],
      commitMessagePrefix: 'feat(github-action)!: ',
    },
    {
      matchManagers: [
        'github-actions',
      ],
      matchUpdateTypes: [
        'minor',
      ],
      semanticCommitType: 'feat',
      semanticCommitScope: 'github-action',
    },
    {
      matchManagers: [
        'github-actions',
      ],
      matchUpdateTypes: [
        'patch',
      ],
      semanticCommitType: 'fix',
      semanticCommitScope: 'github-action',
    },
    {
      matchUpdateTypes: [
        'major',
      ],
      labels: [
        'type/major',
      ],
    },
    {
      matchUpdateTypes: [
        'minor',
      ],
      labels: [
        'type/minor',
      ],
    },
    {
      matchUpdateTypes: [
        'patch',
      ],
      labels: [
        'type/patch',
      ],
    },
    {
      matchDatasources: [
        'docker',
      ],
      addLabels: [
        'renovate/container',
      ],
    },
    {
      matchDatasources: [
        'helm',
      ],
      addLabels: [
        'renovate/helm',
      ],
    },
    {
      matchDatasources: [
        'github-releases',
        'github-tags',
      ],
      addLabels: [
        'renovate/github-release',
      ],
    },
    {
      matchManagers: [
        'github-actions',
      ],
      addLabels: [
        'renovate/github-action',
      ],
    },
  ],
  customManagers: [
    {
      customType: 'regex',
      description: [
        'Process custom dependencies',
      ],
      managerFilePatterns: [
        '/(^|/)kubernetes/.+\\.ya?ml(?:\\.j2)?$/',
      ],
      matchStrings: [
        'datasource=(?<datasource>\\S+) depName=(?<depName>\\S+)( repository=(?<registryUrl>\\S+))?\\n.+: (&\\S+\\s)?(?<currentValue>\\S+)',
      ],
      datasourceTemplate: '{{#if datasource}}{{{datasource}}}{{else}}github-releases{{/if}}',
    },
    {
      customType: 'regex',
      description: [
        "CloudNativePG Cluster imageName - repo:tag combined in one value, unlike the datasource=/depName= comment convention above which needs them split. Confirmed 2026-09-01 this field was invisible to Renovate for the cluster's entire lifetime (never touched since the file was first committed, not even a same-version build-string bump) - CNPG's imageName key isn't the standard \"image:\" key the default docker/kubernetes managers look for.",
      ],
      managerFilePatterns: [
        '/(^|/)kubernetes/.+\\.ya?ml(?:\\.j2)?$/',
      ],
      matchStrings: [
        'imageName:\\s*(?<depName>[^:\\s]+):(?<currentValue>[^\\s@]+)(@(?<currentDigest>sha256:[a-fA-F0-9]+))?',
      ],
      datasourceTemplate: 'docker',
    },
  ],
}
